ion:**   The HPO concept "Micropenis" describes a quantitative anatomical abnormality of the penis—specifically, a penile length below the 5th percentile for age and pubertal stage—reflecting a developmental failure in male genital growth. It is a precise, clinically relevant phenotype primarily rooted in anatomical morphology and developmental biology, with potential links to endocrine or genetic disorders.
