notype with a defined anatomical scope, typically observed in developmental or congenital conditions, and serves as a key feature in the phenotypic characterization of certain genetic or syndromic disorders. Its meaning is grounded in anatomical observation and is used in clinical and research contexts to aid in diagnosis and phenotype-driven gene discovery.
