n:**   The HPO concept "Dyspnea" describes the subjective experience of breathlessness or labored breathing. It is a symptom-level phenotype with broad scope, encompassing various underlying pathologies, and is primarily relevant to respiratory, cardiovascular, and systemic conditions. Its specificity lies in the patient-reported sensation, not in a defined anatomical or biochemical abnormality.
