nary excretion of amino acids due to defective renal reabsorption. It is a broad, clinically significant phenotype with a primary context in renal tubular function and is often a key feature in diagnosing metabolic or genetic disorders affecting amino acid homeostasis. The phenotype is not disease-specific but serves as a phenotypic marker that requires further investigation to determine the underlying cause.
