escribes a structural skeletal deficiency in the hand bones, ranging from complete absence to partial development. It is a specific, anatomically defined phenotype with clinical relevance in developmental biology and congenital disorders, but does not imply functional deficits or involve other tissues. The scope is anatomically precise but lacks granularity on specific bone types—this would be resolved through more specific child terms in the ontology.
