 functional phenotype describing a restricted range of motion in the wrist. It is a clinically observable feature with broad applicability across various diseases and conditions, and its interpretation should be contextualized with additional clinical or genetic data. The concept emphasizes mobility limitation rather than structural damage, making it a key component in phenotypic characterization in genetic and developmental disorders.
