    **Conclusion:**   "Abnormal adipose tissue morphology" denotes a structural deviation in the form or organization of fat tissue, encompassing changes in adipocyte size, tissue architecture, or distribution. It is a descriptive, anatomical-structural phenotype that serves as a foundational observation in phenotypic characterization, particularly in genetic and developmental disorders involving adipose tissue development or integrity.
