y a form of *thumb polydactyly*, and is distinct from syndactyly (fusion of digits) or preaxial polydactyly (extra digits at the thumb side).  **Conclusion:**   The HPO concept "Complete duplication of thumb phalanx" refers to a well-defined, structurally complete extra phalanx in the thumb, representing a specific type of congenital limb malformation. It is anatomically precise, developmentally significant, and clinically relevant in the context of congenital hand anomalies.
