 from preaxial (thumb side) or postaxial (little finger side) polydactyly, as it is defined by the duplication of a bone segment rather than a digit.    **Conclusion:**   The HPO term "Complete duplication of phalanx of hand" describes a rare, fully formed extra phalanx in the hand, representing a specific type of skeletal malformation during limb development. It is anatomically precise, developmentally significant, and clinically relevant in the context of congenital hand anomalies.
