:**   "Aplasia/Hypoplasia of the phalanges of the 4th toe" refers to a specific, localized skeletal defect involving the bony elements of the fourth toe. It is a precise, anatomically defined phenotype with clinical and developmental significance, typically used in the context of congenital disorders affecting limb development.
