ymphalangism" describes a congenital, structural fusion of the distal interphalangeal joint of the second toe, representing a precise anatomical and developmental abnormality. It is a specific, localized skeletal malformation with clear anatomical boundaries and developmental origin, distinct from other forms of toe fusion or joint abnormalities.
