usion:**   "Abnormality of the premaxilla" denotes a structural or developmental deviation in the anterior maxillary bone, specifically affecting the region that supports the upper incisors. It is a broad, anatomically grounded phenotype used in clinical and genetic studies to describe craniofacial malformations, with implications for both developmental biology and clinical diagnosis.
