pecific neurophysiological dysfunction in the ejaculatory reflex pathway. It is a clinically relevant, functionally defined phenotype affecting male reproductive physiology, with a narrow scope focused on timing rather than presence or absence of ejaculation. The concept is best understood as a delay in the physiological process of ejaculation, not a structural or developmental defect.
