obility, representing a functional phenotype that may be a symptom or feature of various underlying diseases or conditions. It is a clinically relevant, anatomically specific, and functionally defined phenotype, with broad applicability across genetic, inflammatory, degenerative, and post-surgical contexts. The concept is not disease-specific but serves as a phenotypic marker for impaired joint mechanics.
