ific diagnosis.  **Conclusion:**   "Ear pain" in HPO refers to the subjective sensation of pain localized to the ear, representing a symptom rather than a disease or structural abnormality. It is a general, symptom-based phenotype with broad scope and clinical relevance, applicable across various etiologies and anatomical regions of the ear. Its specificity is limited by the absence of detailed subtypes or pathophysiological definitions in the current HPO hierarchy.
