re separate phenotypes.  **Conclusion:**   The HPO concept "High serum calcifediol" describes a measurable biochemical abnormality—elevated circulating levels of 25-hydroxyvitamin D—without implying a disease state or clinical symptom. It is a quantitative laboratory finding relevant to vitamin D status and metabolic regulation.
