ogy of the lesions (nummular shape), distinguishing it from other forms of eczema. The absence of a strong association with atopy or systemic features in the HPO definition supports its classification as a distinct dermatological phenotype.  **Conclusion:**   Nummular eczema is a well-defined, localized, chronic inflammatory skin condition characterized by coin-shaped, itchy, scaly patches. It is a cutaneous phenotype with specific morphological and clinical features, primarily affecting the skin, and is distinct from other eczematous disorders based on lesion shape and clinical presentation.
