lar schwannoma, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma).    **Conclusion:**   "Neoplasm of the inner ear" denotes a localized neoplastic process arising in the inner ear structures. It is a precise, anatomically defined pathological phenotype, distinct from other ear or central nervous system neoplasms, and reflects a specific site of abnormal cell growth with implications for hearing and vestibular function.
