ing skeletal development. It is a localized, structural defect affecting a specific anatomical region and is best understood as a developmental anomaly of the distal phalanx. It is not a functional or systemic condition but a morphological feature that may serve as a marker in diagnosing underlying genetic or developmental disorders.
