impaired function, and cosmetic concerns, may be a sign of underlying neuromuscular or connective tissue disorders.  **Conclusion:**   The HPO concept "Contractures of the distal interphalangeal joint of the 5th toe" describes a localized, anatomically precise joint contracture affecting a specific joint in the foot. It is a clinically relevant, specific phenotype used to characterize joint rigidity in the context of genetic, developmental, or degenerative disorders.
