ragment resulting from the enzymatic cleavage of serum albumin. It is a biochemical entity with relevance in physiological and pathological processes involving protein degradation, and it is not a disease phenotype or clinical feature per se. Its scope is narrow and molecular, focused on the product of proteolysis rather than a clinical or developmental abnormality.
