.   - This supports that the core concept is anatomical and developmental, with clinical variants derived from it.  **Conclusion:**   The HPO concept "septum pellucidum" describes the normal or abnormal presence of a specific anatomical structure in the brain. It is a precise, anatomical phenotype related to brain development, with clinical significance primarily in the context of congenital malformations. The phenotype is specific to the central nervous system and reflects structural integrity of the ventricular system.
