ormity* or *Thoracic cage abnormality* in the HPO hierarchy.     - Comment may specify that it is a descriptive morphological feature, not necessarily pathogenic in itself.  **Conclusion:**   "Shield chest" is a morphological phenotype describing a broad, flat, shield-like appearance of the anterior thoracic wall due to abnormal development of the sternum and rib cage. It is a specific anatomical feature with clinical relevance in the context of congenital skeletal disorders and is best understood as a structural thoracic abnormality, distinct from functional or symptomatic manifestations.
