tis" describes a chronic inflammatory skin condition that manifests in adolescence or adulthood, with clinical features consistent with atopic dermatitis but with a delayed onset. It is a specific, clinically relevant phenotype within the broader spectrum of atopic disorders, emphasizing timing of onset as a key differentiator.
